      "generated_by": "llamacpp",
      "segment_index": 1,
      "segment_title": "Part 1",
      "canonical_line_id": "canonical_v0001_line_0005_7c101166"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "phil",
      "text": "Oh! So the problem isn't just about having more tools, but each tool being more specialized for specific models? That makes sense.",
      "emotion": "warm",
      "pause_after": 0.35,
      "rhythm": {
        "human_load": 0.45,
        "desync_risk": 0.448,
        "turn_latency_ms": 0.0,
        "tempo": "normal",
        "intensity": "medium",
        "verbosity": "medium",
        "cooldown_until_ms": 1791293139759,
        "version": 1,
        "interaction_tempo": "normal",
        "cognitive_intensity": "medium",
        "last_turn_ms": 0.0
      },
      "line_number": 6,
      "generated_by": "llamacpp",
      "segment_index": 1,
      "segment_title": "Part 1",
      "canonical_line_id": "canonical_v0001_line_0006_bdd5e40e"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "jim",
      "text": "Exactly. Each car model might have its own unique software configuration. So if I fix a Tesla with a key fob, it doesn't help when I try to fix my SUV because the diagnostics are",
      "emotion": "neutral",
      "pause_after": 0.55,
      "rhythm": {
        "human_load": 0.45,
        "desync_risk": 0.448,
        "turn_latency_ms": 0.0,
        "tempo": "normal",
        "intensity": "medium",
        "verbosity": "medium",
        "cooldown_until_ms": 1791293139759,
        "version": 1,
        "interaction_tempo": "normal",
        "cognitive_intensity": "medium",
        "last_turn_ms": 0.0
      },
      "line_number": 7,
      "generated_by": "llamacpp",
      "segment_index": 1,
      "segment_title": "Part 1",
      "canonical_line_id": "canonical_v0001_line_0007_0d985a6e"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "phil",
      "text": "Interesting! It must be frustrating for mechanics to keep up with all these changes without proper training or access to updated diagnostic equipment.",
      "emotion": "warm",
      "pause_after": 0.35,
      "rhythm": {
        "human_load": 0.45,
        "desync_risk": 0.448,
        "turn_latency_ms": 0.0,
        "tempo": "normal",
        "intensity": "medium",
        "verbosity": "medium",
        "cooldown_until_ms": 1791293139759,
        "version": 1,
        "interaction_tempo": "normal",
        "cognitive_intensity": "medium",
        "last_turn_ms": 0.0
      },
      "line_number": 8,
      "generated_by": "llamacpp",
      "segment_index": 1,
      "segment_title": "Part 1",
      "canonical_line_id": "canonical_v0001_line_0008_f0e6720a"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "phil",
      "text": "So if a car manufacturer updates its software, does that mean all existing mechanics lose access to the old diagnostics? That's scary because I know people who still use the same",
      "emotion": "warm",
      "pause_after": 0.35,
      "rhythm": {
        "human_load": 0.45,
        "desync_risk": 0.448,
        "turn_latency_ms": 0.0,
        "tempo": "normal",
        "intensity": "medium",
        "verbosity": "medium",
        "cooldown_until_ms": 1791293139759,
        "version": 1,
        "interaction_tempo": "normal",
        "cognitive_intensity": "medium",
        "last_turn_ms": 0.0
      },
      "line_number": 9,
      "generated_by": "llamacpp",
      "segment_index": 1,
      "segment_title": "Part 1",
      "canonical_line_id": "canonical_v0001_line_0009_28c7745d"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "jim",
      "text": "Exactly! Updates are usually backward incompatible with older diagnostic tools. So when Tesla updated their software for Model S, owners couldn't use their old key fobs anymore. It",
      "emotion": "neutral",
      "pause_after": 0.55,
      "rhythm": {
        "human_load": 0.45,
        "desync_risk": 0.448,
        "turn_latency_ms": 0.0,
        "tempo": "normal",
        "intensity": "medium",
        "verbosity": "medium",
        "cooldown_until_ms": 1791293139759,
        "version": 1,
        "interaction_tempo": "normal",
        "cognitive_intensity": "medium",
        "last_turn_ms": 0.0
      },
      "line_number": 10,
      "generated_by": "llamacpp",
      "segment_index": 1,
      "segment_title": "Part 1",
      "canonical_line_id": "canonical_v0001_line_0010_eda056fe"
    },
    {
      "speaker": "phil",
      "text": "That makes a lot of sense now. I can see how manufacturers would prioritize keeping the latest diagnostics to prevent issues and ensure compatibility without disrupting existing",
      "emotion": "warm",
      "pause_after": 0.35,
      "rhythm": {
        "human_load": 0.45,
        "desync_risk": 0.448,
        "turn_latency_ms": 0.0,
        "tempo": "normal",
        "intensity": "medium",
        "verbosity": "medium",
        "cooldown_until_ms": 1791293139759,
        "version": 1,
        "interaction_tempo": "normal",
        "cognitive_intensity": "medium",
        "last_turn_ms": 0.0
      },
